Put $E=T_B(-\log D)$. There is a flat complex identification of $U_X$ with a character eigenspace having Hodge components $$\label{geom:hodge-eigensheaves}
 U_X^{p,q}\simeq
 H^q\bigl(B,\Omega_B^p(\log D)\otimes M^{-1}\chi\bigr),
 \qquad p+q=2.$$ In particular, $U_X^{2,0}=H^0(B,M\chi)$ is one-dimensional. Fix a nonzero translation-invariant volume form $\Omega$ on $B$, and let $\theta\in H^0(B,M\chi)$ represent this line. Under <a href="#geom:hodge-eigensheaves" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="geom:hodge-eigensheaves">[geom:hodge-eigensheaves]</a>, the period differential is the map on $H^1$ induced by $$\label{geom:derivative}
 E\xrightarrow{\ \theta\ }E\otimes M\chi
       \simeq\Omega_B^1(\log D)\otimes M^{-1}\chi.$$ The Kodaira–Spencer map identifies the tangent space of the full six-dimensional family $(B,M,\chi,[d])$ with $H^1(B,E)$.

Let $f:\mathcal Z\to B$ be a smooth proper holomorphic family of pure relative dimension $n$ over a connected coordinate ball, with a closed relative embedding $\mathcal Z\subset\mathbf P^N\times B$. Fix an integer $0\leq r\leq n$, a rational local system $\mathcal V$ on $B$, a morphism of local systems $$L:R^{2r}f_*\mathbb Q\longrightarrow\mathcal V,$$ and a flat section $\tau$ of $\mathcal V$. The set of $b\in B$ admitting a rational codimension-$r$ algebraic cycle $Z_b$ such that $$\label{final:cycle-condition}
 L_b\bigl(\mathop{\mathrm{cl}}(Z_b)\bigr)=\tau_b$$ is a countable union of closed analytic subsets of $B$. Each subset in this union is the image of a proper analytic parameter space carrying a fixed rational combination of universal flat subschemes; every point of that space supplies a cycle satisfying <a href="#final:cycle-condition" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="final:cycle-condition">[final:cycle-condition]</a>.*

*If the successful set contains a nonempty open subset of $B$, it equals $B$. The same conclusion holds if, for every countable union of proper closed analytic subsets of $B$, there is a successful point outside that union.
